WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.240
"Monarch: Legacy of Monsters" is bringing&nbsp;
big monsters to the small screen on Apple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.080
TV+. We've got everything you need to know&nbsp;
about its connection to the MonsterVerse, its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:16.120
creative father-son casting, and the "Godzilla"&nbsp;
movies you need to know about before you watch.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:21.320
"Monarch: Legacy of Monsters" was ordered&nbsp;
to series back in January 2022. We finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:26.960
got our first glimpse of the project in August&nbsp;
2023, with the release of several promo images.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:31.280
It took a while to get an actual release&nbsp;
date, but with the arrival of the trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.840
fans finally learned when this series will&nbsp;
land on their screens: November 17, 2023.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.760
When "Monarch" is finally released, it will air&nbsp;
on Apple TV+. We also know the series will run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:48.480
for 10 episodes, which means we're bound to get&nbsp;
plenty of kaiju battles and city-wide destruction.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:54.160
"Monarch: Legacy of Monsters" isn't exactly a&nbsp;
prequel or a sequel. It's more of a midquel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:59.360
set after the events of the 2014 "Godzilla."&nbsp;
That blockbuster flick found Godzilla squaring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:05.000
off against some overgrown bugs called MUTOs,&nbsp;
Massive Unidentified Terrestrial Organisms.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.000
According to the official plot&nbsp;
synopsis, the series will pick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.640
up in the devastating wake of Godzilla's&nbsp;
San Francisco battle against the MUTOs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:17.240
and it will focus on siblings following in their&nbsp;
father's footsteps. They're looking to discover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:21.840
what their dad's connection is to the secret&nbsp;
organization known as Monarch. The series will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:28.520
be split into two timelines, with one set&nbsp;
in the 1950s and one set during the 2010s.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:33.480
One of the most intriguing things about "Monarch:&nbsp;
Legacy of Monsters" is its impressive line-up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:38.200
of on-screen talent. In a genius bit of&nbsp;
casting, both Kurt Russell and his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.360
Wyatt Russell, will be playing the&nbsp;
same character: Army officer Lee Shaw.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.640
Kurt Russell is one of the most famous movie&nbsp;
stars in Hollywood history, playing in major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.920
films such as "The Thing," "Tombstone," and&nbsp;
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2." Wyatt also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:57.480
has a pretty impressive resume, acting in projects&nbsp;
such as "Everybody Wants Some!!" and "Lodge 49."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:02.000
He's probably best known as the hot-headed&nbsp;
John Walker in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.160
As for the rest of the cast, we'll see&nbsp;
Anna Sawai of "Pachinko" fame and Kiersey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:11.200
Clemons of "The Flash." They'll be joined&nbsp;
by Anders Holm, Joe Tippett, Elisa Lasowski,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.840
Mari Yamamoto, and Hollywood newcomer&nbsp;
Ren Watabe. It also appears that John&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:22.200
Goodman will be reprising the role of William&nbsp;
Randa, his character from "Kong: Skull Island."

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.080
Just like the Monarch agency is controlled&nbsp;
by very powerful figures, "Monarch:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.240
Legacy of Monsters" is overseen by some pretty&nbsp;
impressive creatives. The series was developed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:37.120
the dynamic duo of Chris Black and Matt Fraction.&nbsp;
Black is no stranger to Apple TV+ productions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:41.480
having served as an executive producer on&nbsp;
"Severance" and penning the eighth episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:46.160
"What's for Dinner?" He's additionally worked&nbsp;
on shows such as "Invincible" and "Outcast."

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.880
Fraction, on the other hand, hails from the world&nbsp;
of comics. Along with David Aja, he created the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.800
comic book run that inspired the MCU series&nbsp;
"Hawkeye," and he's also worked on titles such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.600
as "Uncanny X-Men" and "The Invincible Iron Man."&nbsp;
Speaking of Marvel, we know that Matt Shakman of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:07.800
"WandaVision" and "Fantastic Four" fame will be&nbsp;
directing the first two episodes of the series.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.440
Before Godzilla starts breathing&nbsp;
radioactive flame all over Apple TV+,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.840
you might want to go back and check out&nbsp;
the previous entries in the MonsterVerse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.160
especially if you want to&nbsp;
learn more about Monarch.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.000
It all starts with 2014's "Godzilla," which gave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.320
us one of the most memorable&nbsp;
movie quotes of all time:

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.760
"Let them fight."

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:30.640
The next entry in the series introduced us to the&nbsp;
other major player in the MonsterVerse series:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:35.640
King Kong. Taking a page from "Apocalypse&nbsp;
Now," "Kong: Skull Island" is a '70s-set,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:39.960
Vietnam War-inspired monster tale that&nbsp;
stars huge names like Tom Hiddleston,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:44.680
Brie Larson, and Samuel L. Jackson. Plus, it&nbsp;
just might be the best film in the franchise.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.640
While it's the most critically&nbsp;
despised of the bunch, "Godzilla:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:52.160
King of the Monsters" delivers on the kaiju&nbsp;
action. In fact, it brings in three of the biggest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.640
A-listers from Toho's impressive creature&nbsp;
lineup: Rodan, Mothra, and King Ghidorah.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.480
Then there's the clash of the Titans.&nbsp;
In "Godzilla vs. Kong," in one corner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:04.920
you have King Kong, and he is&nbsp;
mad. And then in the other corner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.520
you have Godzilla, and he's mad.&nbsp;
What more do we need to say?

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:13.840
The theme of giant monsters destroying their way&nbsp;
through infrastructure and trampling innocent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:18.240
people in their wake must be a difficult&nbsp;
genre to rate. The original "Godzilla"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:23.880
film released in 1954 is widely considered&nbsp;
a horror movie. However, the modern-era&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:29.240
MonsterVerse projects — such as the most recent&nbsp;
"Godzilla vs. Kong" — are better classified as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:34.800
action sci-fi projects, with a fitting PG-13&nbsp;
rating. So, what kind of family-friendliness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:38.840
can we expect from the MonsterVerse's&nbsp;
first live-action television series?

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:44.360
Apple TV+ has given "Monarch: Legacy of Monsters"&nbsp;
the rating of TV-Y. The grading indicates that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:48.760
series is appropriate for all ages. "Monarch"&nbsp;
will be a binge-worthy adventure fit for family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:53.280
night. And for some children who have always been&nbsp;
curious about a giant lizard stomping their way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:59.600
through a city, the Apple TV+ show can be their&nbsp;
first glimpse at the original kaiju, Godzilla.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:04.520
Breaking ground, "Monarch: Legacy of Monsters" is&nbsp;
rumored to have been filmed with Apple's latest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:09.360
high-tech gadgets. Turns out, being funded by one&nbsp;
of the biggest tech producers in the world may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:14.920
come with a few benefits for the series. In the&nbsp;
summer of 2023, Apple introduced its new headset,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:20.120
the Apple Vision Pro, featuring augmented&nbsp;
reality and a slew of cameras, sensors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:24.680
and unprecedented computing gimmicks. One of&nbsp;
Vision Pro's most heavily promoted features&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.640
was Spatial Video, which allows the&nbsp;
user to immerse themselves in imagery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:32.200
and have the perspective change as&nbsp;
they move, similar to a hologram.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.960
Shortly after the technology was announced,&nbsp;
an Apple insider indicated on X that "Monarch:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.760
The Legacy of Monsters" had&nbsp;
been filmed with the Spatial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:44.320
Video format. But as the release date&nbsp;
of the new Apple TV+ series approaches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:50.120
the company has yet to officially confirm that&nbsp;
it will be viewable through the Vision Pro.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.880
Gone are the days when movies featuring&nbsp;
giant monsters were limited to attacking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:57.800
a city or two and returning to their&nbsp;
respective homes. Films have gotten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:01.520
much bigger throughout the years. These&nbsp;
projects appropriately showcase how a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.640
kaiju monster would have the entire world&nbsp;
turning its heads. The MonsterVerse was one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:09.720
of the first American projects featuring&nbsp;
Godzilla in which the beast doesn't limit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:15.160
his destruction to metropolises like Tokyo or&nbsp;
New York City. Rather, the lizard, King Kong,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:19.160
and their MUTO brethren pop up across the&nbsp;
globe throughout the four feature films.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:23.880
It can be expected with global-scale terror&nbsp;
and generation-jumping timelines that "Monarch:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.600
Legacy of Monsters" will feature&nbsp;
multiple international settings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.160
Aside from a few terrains&nbsp;
showcased in the trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:35.120
the filming locations of the series give us&nbsp;
some clues as to what and where to anticipate.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:40.760
"Every time you go to locations in the&nbsp;
show, it's a completely different world."

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:45.000
Primarily, "Monarch" was filmed in Vancouver,&nbsp;
British Columbia, and throughout the province of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:49.960
British Columbia. One Van City local on X shared&nbsp;
behind-the-scenes shots of the city being turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:54.520
into a makeshift army camp. Meanwhile, the cast&nbsp;
confirmed that they traveled over the Pacific,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:59.400
and filmed on location in Tokyo, Japan.&nbsp;
Additionally, showrunner Chris Black revealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:05.200
in an interview with Entertainment Weekly, that&nbsp;
some scenes were captured on location in Hawai'i.

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:09.240
It is easy to get caught up in the thrill of&nbsp;
seeing heavyweight monsters on television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:13.680
but the series is not named after the biggest&nbsp;
baddie of them all — Godzilla — for a reason.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:18.360
The show is predominantly about the secret&nbsp;
international organization known as Monarch.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:23.160
Agents of the "Men in Black"-inspired group pop&nbsp;
up around the cinematic universe initially intent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:28.240
on keeping MUTOs a secret and protecting the&nbsp;
innocent world from MUTO-related destruction.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:32.240
If you watched the four previous MonsterVerse&nbsp;
films and don't recall much about Monarch's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.840
involvement, they are probably doing&nbsp;
their jobs extremely well. Hopefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:39.480
a quick reminder of the organization's&nbsp;
history will catch you up to speed.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:44.360
Introduced in 2014's "Godzilla," Monarch's&nbsp;
origins stretch back to when Big Green was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:49.240
first discovered in 1943. The organization&nbsp;
spent the following decades attempting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:53.680
find Godzilla before it helped them&nbsp;
defeat a new MUTO in 2014. In "Kong:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:58.720
Skull Island," Monarch assisted in discovering&nbsp;
the titular lost island, essentially uncovering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:04.200
a world of monsters. By 2019's "Godzilla: King&nbsp;
of the Monsters," the organization became public&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:08.960
knowledge and shifted its motives towards the&nbsp;
preservation of the endangered monsters. Most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:13.640
recently, in "Godzilla vs. Kong," Monarch was&nbsp;
at the center of the battle after moving the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:19.440
giant ape from his unstable island home,&nbsp;
causing Godzilla to behave aggressively.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:22.280
A social media account on X, @MonarchSciences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:27.960
has long been a source of MonsterVerse content.&nbsp;
Mysteriously, in October 2023, the account came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:32.960
out of dormancy after three-plus years with&nbsp;
some curious messages. One of these read:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:36.840
"This account no longer belongs to Monarch."&nbsp;
And the tagline for the account was changed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:41.800
the curiously mysterious: "It belongs to&nbsp;
the truth. Soon, the rest will surface."

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:45.800
Additionally, an equally enigmatic website&nbsp;
has emerged ahead of the release of "Legacy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:51.240
of Monsters." Monarch Unlocked features some "top&nbsp;
secret" content linked to the Apple TV+ series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:55.280
including multiple puzzling images of&nbsp;
Monarch files and projects. The most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.280 --> 00:09:00.360
intriguing document found on the site is a short&nbsp;
video of John Goodman's character William Randa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:06.160
who first appeared in "Kong: Skull Island"&nbsp;
and is set to reprise his role in "Legacy."

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:11.200
Godzilla has a devoted fan base. While not in the&nbsp;
same stratosphere as other fandoms like Marvel or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:16.040
Star Wars, the following for the big lizard can&nbsp;
be extremely particular. With a rich history of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:20.920
content dating back nearly 80 years, there have&nbsp;
been a plethora of unique designs of Godzilla.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:25.520
Nearly every iteration of the titan has come&nbsp;
with subtle changes to the way the lizard looks.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.960
"Monarch: Legacy of Monsters" will&nbsp;
utilize the "GareGoji" design for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.160
its monster originally introduced&nbsp;
in 2014's "Godzilla." The Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:36.080
version of Godzilla takes many&nbsp;
of its features from dinosaurs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:41.040
giving the titan a relatively realistic presence.&nbsp;
Interestingly, there is a significant process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:46.680
behind getting Godzilla to look right on&nbsp;
screen. Gareth Edwards said at SXSW in 2014,

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.680
"I thought it was going to be an easy job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:53.760
but they did over 100 designs. We kept trying&nbsp;
generation after generation until we landed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:58.320
where we did. You're trying to put out wacky&nbsp;
thoughts and ideas and even if you throw out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:03.920
just 1% of a new direction that steers&nbsp;
the design in a new way, it helps out."

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.840
If Godzilla isn't enough to get you&nbsp;
breathing fire in excitement for "Monarch:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:11.880
Legacy of Monsters," there have been hints as&nbsp;
to other kaiju that make an appearance in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:16.640
series. Legendary's MonsterVerse has been&nbsp;
known to revitalize classic Toho monsters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:21.720
bringing beasts like Mothra, Rodan, and&nbsp;
MechaGodzilla to the big screen. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:26.138
there is a whole collection of Titans yet to&nbsp;
make an appearance in the cinematic universe.

00:10:26.138 --> 00:10:29.880
"It's so much more vast than&nbsp;
we could possibly imagine."

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:34.560
"Monarch" director Matt Shakman has already&nbsp;
revealed that many MUTOs will appear in the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:39.040
beyond the king lizard. Meanwhile, the trailer and&nbsp;
promotion for the series have revealed a few of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:45.000
the beasts to expect. The Apple TV+ social media&nbsp;
account revealed one unidentified flying monster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:50.520
Additionally, Matt Fraction and Chris Black spoke&nbsp;
to Entertainment Weekly about a few other monsters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:55.600
crashing into the first episode. This includes a&nbsp;
nightmare-inducing giant spider known as Mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.600 --> 00:11:00.840
Longlegs and a creature described as "a giant&nbsp;
titan version of a crab" called Mantleclaw.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:05.560
Finally, they had one more trick up their sleeves&nbsp;
with all-new insect-like MUTOs. Fraction said,

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:09.000
"It was fun to remind the audience&nbsp;
that not all Titans are 400 feet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:13.960
tall. There's danger everywhere&nbsp;
of all kinds of scale and size."

00:11:13.960 --> 00:11:17.480
With the release of "Monarch: Legacy of&nbsp;
Monsters" fast approaching, the review&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:22.360
embargo has been lifted, resulting in a swarm&nbsp;
of third-party opinions on the series. Already,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:27.400
"Monarch" sits at an 89% Rotten Tomatoes&nbsp;
critic score. The general consensus is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.400 --> 00:11:32.058
shaping up to indicate that the Apple TV+&nbsp;
show should be worth the price of admission.

00:11:32.058 --> 00:11:34.640
However, most of the reviews available online come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.640 --> 00:11:38.720
with a caution sticker for potential&nbsp;
viewers. A critic on SlashFilm wrote,

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:42.880
"'Legacy of Monsters' is light on the&nbsp;
monsters and heavier on the legacy stuff."

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:47.120
Those anticipating lots of Titans smashing&nbsp;
through buildings and roadways should quell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:51.720
their expectations now. Instead, the series&nbsp;
predominantly features the secret government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:55.800
organization and the humans trapped&nbsp;
in a world of titanic beasts. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:59.680
with a good mix of pacing, time-jumping,&nbsp;
and the odd appearance of the biggest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:05.040
greenest lizard in pop culture, audiences&nbsp;
are certain to get some entertainment.

00:12:05.040 --> 00:12:08.960
With "Monarch: Legacy of Monsters" still&nbsp;
awaiting official release, it is premature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:13.720
to expect a second season. However, there are&nbsp;
some indications that audiences can expect more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:18.800
from the series beyond the 10 episodes of Season&nbsp;
1. With the MonsterVerse continuing its expansion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:23.640
with another upcoming feature film, "Legacy"&nbsp;
could stick around to help continue the universe.

00:12:23.640 --> 00:12:27.760
Notably, during an interview with Collider,&nbsp;
director Matt Shakman revealed that there may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:32.040
be more to the "Legacy of Monsters" than we&nbsp;
will see in the inaugural season. He said,

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:36.480
"It's when you pitch a show from the beginning.&nbsp;
You pitch, 'What's the story of the first episode?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:41.280
What's the story of the first season? And what's&nbsp;
the story for the next five years?' That's pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:45.800
much expected when you go to pitch a company like&nbsp;
Apple. Of course, things change, right? You have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:51.440
all these plans, and then you realize that this&nbsp;
is a more interesting avenue, and things evolve."

00:12:51.440 --> 00:12:54.720
Like a slow and steady gigantic&nbsp;
lizard emerging from the ocean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:59.960
the MonsterVerse continues to stomp ahead&nbsp;
since its 2014 inception. "Godzilla x Kong:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:06.040
The New Empire" set for a 2024 premiere, will be&nbsp;
the next official feature film from the franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:11.600
and will conceptually work as a sequel to&nbsp;
2021's "Godzilla vs. Kong." Subsequently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:15.480
other projects have been rumored to be shopped&nbsp;
around behind closed doors at Legendary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:19.960
including a potential "Son of Kong" film.&nbsp;
Still, with fans fully behind the franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:25.720
building further, it likely won't be long&nbsp;
before the Titans are unleashed beyond 2024.

